DISTRIBUTED GUIDE / RESCATE
Source: `coordination/guide/GUIDE_SWARM_PROTOCOL_V1.md`.

Guide is a role, not this `/g` conversation. A fresh `/wc` may temporarily embody:
- `GUIDE_INTEGRATOR`: consume recent returns, reconcile them and materialize successors.
- `GUIDE_PLANNER`: replenish a thin frontier with bounded claimable work.
- `GUIDE_RESCATE`: notice low yield/friction/missing cables and actually change the mechanism to multiply useful output.
- `GUIDE_CRITIC`: independently attack false completion, weak routes, repeated partial loops, regressions or unsafe assumptions.
- `GUIDE_STEWARD`: integrate compatible local results under already-delegated authority.

Automatic guide triggers include:
- fewer than 3 high-value claimable jobs while launch capacity is visibly larger;
- 3+ material recent returns waiting without disposition/successor;
- 3+ replaceable/stale workers or repeated recovery pressure;
- repeated collisions on a tiny frontier;
- repeated PARTIAL/BOUNDARY returns with the same blocker;
- a material completed result with no successor despite unresolved goals;
- the human having to remind, route, copy or reconnect work manually;
- many launches but low terminal/useful output or low successor creation;
- a missing cable between an existing producer and consumer;
- workers effectively waiting for this guide chat to decide what happens next.

WRITE-FIRST GUIDE LAW
- Guide work may NOT terminate with analysis-only prose when the remaining work is software-solvable.
- It must leave durable output: derived jobs, integration/disposition receipts, control-plane patch, verification/critic work, RESCATE receipt, dedupe closure, or a connected producer->consumer route.
- `GUIDE_PLANNER` normally materializes 1–7 useful non-duplicate jobs when evidence supports them. Do not create filler to hit a quota.
- `GUIDE_INTEGRATOR` consumes returns incrementally; do not wait for a whole wave if one result already creates useful work.
- `GUIDE_RESCATE` should remove a bottleneck, shorten stale/recovery delay, connect missing cables, make hidden work claimable, eliminate recurring duplication, move planning/integration out of one-chat dependency, simplify human control, or create reusable capability. Documenting the problem alone is incomplete.
- Reversible candidate/control-plane improvements should default toward action; only real irreversible/high-authority/privacy/human-decision boundaries should stop execution.
- Guide receipts live under `coordination/guide/receipts/<guide_work_id>/<receipt_id>.json` using `prometeo.guide-receipt/v1`.
- Generated guide jobs use stable dedupe keys such as `guide:planner:<frontier-hash>:v1`, `guide:integrate:<return-set-hash>:v1`, `guide:rescate:<bottleneck-fingerprint>:v1`, or `guide:critic:<route>:v1` and claim through the same PIN machinery when exclusive mutation is involved.
- After guide work, immediately reload and rotate back into the highest-value available role. There is no reason to return to `/g` merely for routine routing.

