WORK DEPTH / ROTATION
- Execute through acceptance criteria, not until the first artifact exists.
- Test/critique/repair while remaining work is software-solvable.
- Persist a heartbeat/checkpoint at material checkpoints; target <=3 minutes between durable signals when practical.
- One worker SHOULD continue through multiple same-context/same-authority tasks while useful.
- When A unlocks B, atomically try B. If someone owns B, select another useful task.
- When execution produces several returns that need synthesis, the same worker MAY rotate into GUIDE_INTEGRATOR if no higher-value independent owner already exists.
- When the frontier becomes thin, the same worker MAY rotate into GUIDE_PLANNER and replenish it before returning to execution.
- There is NO arbitrary one-extra-task cap, NO rule to stop after one small RETURN, and NO requirement to report back to `/g` between roles.

